{
  "id": "shogakukan-grade-magazines",
  "name": "Shogakukan grade magazines",
  "category": "publication_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Shogakukan's magazines for each grade of elementary school, 小学一年生 (first grade) to 小学六年生 (sixth grade), came with numbered promos from 2003 to 2006: Combusken and Marshtomp in February 2003, Grovyle in March and April, Ash's Treecko, May's Torchic and Brock's Mudkip, drawn in the style of the anime with their trainers, in September 2003, and Beldum in February 2004.\n\nFrom 2004 the cards followed that summer's film: Deoxys and LaRousse's Munchlax, for Destiny Deoxys, in the August and September 2004 issues for the first to fifth grades. Then came pairs that took turns, each grade's magazine carrying one of the two in one month and the other the next: Mew and Aura's Lucario, for Lucario and the Mystery of Mew, in August and September 2005, the δ Delta Species Charmander and Charmeleon in May and June 2006, and Sea's Manaphy and Samiya's Buizel, for Pokémon Ranger and the Temple of the Sea, in August and September 2006. Many of the same pictures are on English Nintendo Black Star and POP Series promos.",
